      "writtenOn": "2020-10-01T00:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. This is correct.\n\nTo be precise, debugd (which is userspace instead of kernel, though still AP-land) calls `ectool usbpd` when we collect debug logs.\n\nWhat we\u0027re looking for is a single command for debugd to use, regardless of TCPM variant; if we have a way to have a single command work, that would be preferred i.e we can change debugd to call `ectool typec-status`.\n\nFWIW, I think the current `ectool usbpd` changes its output depending on USB_PD_CONTROL command version, so this wouldn\u0027t be much different.",
      "parentUuid": "9f15678e_d7aee6ab",
      "revId": "ab36ed788678645dbc868157a3ca6e32422db88f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
